{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195292-avoid-falling-unconcious","id":195292,"title":"Avoid falling unconcious","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-11T23:34:46-07:00","id":195292,"title":"Avoid falling unconcious","content":"sorry if this has been posted before but i didn't find anything in the search function about it.<br /> <br /> i'm starting a new homebrew setting using the cwod rules and the characters for the most part will be human and have a question about bashing damage.<br /> in cwod what if anything does a player do once his health track is full of bashing damage to avoid being rendered unconscious?<br /> do they roll their willpower? spend willpower per turn? roll some other stat?<br /> in nwod i know its the composure roll but can't figure out an equivalent in cwod.<br /> <br /> thanks for any help in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T23:49:25-07:00","id":195302,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking? Nothing.<br /> <br /> Though theoretically you could interpret the WP rules to allow you to stay conscious for 1 turn/WP but it isn't going to do you much good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:27:33-07:00","id":195797,"title":"","content":"i thought as much<br /> thanks for confirming.<br /> probably talk to my co-dm of some homebrew rules of maybe letting players fight off unconsciousness with some roles and spending wp points.<br /> <br /> but how do people find it who have played human centered games before in wod dealing with the frailties of humans?<br /> my experience thus far has always been with vampire characters whom just spend blood to heal bashing dmg constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:50:56-07:00","id":195809,"title":"","content":"I've played a human-only setting, but as the theme was heavily inspired by Silent Hill and its ilk, going mad was a bigger danger than being wounded. Any human campaign that regularly has the potential to wound PCs should better plan for some serious amount of downtime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T01:36:44-07:00","id":196136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195292-avoid-falling-unconcious?p=195797#post195797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but how do people find it who have played human centered games before in wod dealing with the frailties of humans?<br /> my experience thus far has always been with vampire characters whom just spend blood to heal bashing dmg constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen much interest in playing normal morals in the cWOD because the system is so biased against them. One of things the nWOD accomplished with little dispute is making playing normal humans in the WOD a more desirable mode of play.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a &quot;mortals plus&quot; style cWOD game with material like Hunters Hunted, Sorcerer, or even Hunter the Reckoning, there's enough oomph available to the PCs to not being so easily shut down in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T02:05:23-07:00","id":196154,"title":"","content":"I've both played and ST'd my fair share of Mortal games, some of which admittedly have changed to supernatural games at some point, and in my experience the frailties of humans are what makes these games so human. That is to say it keeps players from going full on Action Movie style gameplay as one hit may disable their character for a long while. Mortal games are good at teaching people to play smart, avoid violence and duck &amp; cover. After all how often do you engage a life threatening combat or combat in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T17:38:38-07:00","id":197277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195292-avoid-falling-unconcious?p=196136#post196136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never seen much interest in playing normal morals in the cWOD because the system is so biased against them. One of things the nWOD accomplished with little dispute is making playing normal humans in the WOD a more desirable mode of play.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a &quot;mortals plus&quot; style cWOD game with material like Hunters Hunted, Sorcerer, or even Hunter the Reckoning, there's enough oomph available to the PCs to not being so easily shut down in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the setting i'm creating is a humans only dystopian sci-fi future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T17:41:30-07:00","id":197278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195292-avoid-falling-unconcious?p=196154#post196154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've both played and ST'd my fair share of Mortal games, some of which admittedly have changed to supernatural games at some point, and in my experience the frailties of humans are what makes these games so human. That is to say it keeps players from going full on Action Movie style gameplay as one hit may disable their character for a long while. Mortal games are good at teaching people to play smart, avoid violence and duck &amp; cover. After all how often do you engage a life threatening combat or combat in general?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i did notice that too actually when i started making this setting and thinking of the players playing as humans. most of the time in wod rules we've always played vampires and healing damage was trivial to them when facing off against humans and ghouls and such.<br /> frankly i do like the idea of the brutality level of it and will have to see where it goes.<br /> i am giving players a chance to keep from falling unconscious though and since it's sci-fi i can make some tech maguffins that give some of the powers that are like those in vampire and hunters but i need to work with my co-dm to make sure they all fit with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T20:54:41-07:00","id":197385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195292-avoid-falling-unconcious?p=197277#post197277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the setting i'm creating is a humans only dystopian sci-fi future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the cWOD, but the nWOD has a lot more support for this already. Is there a reason you want to keep to the cWOD for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T20:32:46-07:00","id":207855,"title":"","content":"hmmm none really other than i don't have the nwod books.<br /> i've always avoided them, since i preferred the cwod storyline more than requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T02:31:53-07:00","id":208048,"title":"","content":"If you're worrying about humans being hurt and having to spend a bunch of time healing, Mage has rules for improving healing times. I think if you're being tended by someone with Medicine 4+, your healing times are halved. Though I'd just make each 2 successes on a medicine roll from the performing Doctor reduce the healing time by a factor of two or something. Healing is a pain. Even being able to heal bashing damage in under a week is valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T15:03:22-07:00","id":208734,"title":"","content":"pretty much what i figured.<br /> but i've been talking with my co-dm and we agree that a brutal setting (sci-fi noir punk) would actually be quite nice. especially after the games we've been having lately. l5r heal times are hilarious.<br /> also since it is a sci-fi setting i've basically created an equivalent of a bacta tank and also nano healing bot injectors and things that should make healing go much faster.<br /> but it will be nice to make the players think like regular humans for a change instead of super powered freaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}